      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It won’t really work, especially since more and more countries around the world are trying to introduce age restrictions for online services. These regulations usually all have the same core idea: verify the user’s personal data.\n\nAn account itself could already be 18 years old, which would mean you know the person is an adult. Lawmakers still require a separate verification, though.\n\nSo it doesn’t make any sense to build a system now that relies on the age of the account.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-12-20T07:59:51.072Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Despite widespread support for age verification on social platforms, the devil is always in the details. The majority of people are not in favor of handing over their IDs to access R18/NSFW content, and requiring it causes alienation. But we still want people to be able to access things when they're legally allowed to, so I think proactively attempting to shave off the need for such a thing in any area possible is a good thing. One such area came to mind:\n\nAccounts that are themselves old enough that the owner of said account would be old enough to get age verification. I think they should be age verified automatically.\n\nFor most countries the age of majority is 18, and since VRChat's TOS says that the creator of an account must be 13+, the math for that comes out such that any account that's 5+ years old would get age verified automatically. I expect this would get implemented regionally though, since there are many with different ages of majority. Simple geolocation would probably suffice.\n\nIf anyone is found abusing this, e.g. by sharing accounts, their accounts simply get banned, just like with any other form of age verification.",
